{
	title: 'Optional Codex and Claude command-hook adapters',
	spec: 'Optional native plugins in extras adapt explicitly selected Codex and Claude hook configuration and local plugin packages, without loading compatibility machinery in core. Commands require explicit trust for the exact configuration content; changed definitions never execute until reviewed again. Support useful pre-tool denial and post-tool feedback/context with published event mappings and honest unsupported coverage. Package hook paths stay inside package roots including symlinks. Reject unsupported handler/event semantics visibly rather than silently bypassing policies. Run command hooks with JSON stdin, timeouts and cancellation; capture full failures without terminal writes. Keep fixture tests for trust, package containment, event input/output and blocking behavior. Document installation, opt-in, supported package components and limitations.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Official Codex hooks, OpenAI plugin packaging, Claude hooks and manifest references checked 2026-10-24. Codex now supports root portable plugin.json extensions[com.openai], with .codex-plugin fallback; explicit hooks replaces default. Claude inline hooks are event maps and merge with default hooks/hooks.json. Matchers differ: Claude simple names/lists exact, Codex regex. These distinctions have fixture coverage.',
		'Scope: optional extras/codex-hooks.ts and claude-hooks.ts share hook-sources.ts, hook-command.ts, command-hooks.ts; no core edits or automatic discovery. SessionStart and UserPromptSubmit run at awaited request boundaries, pre/post tools at tools.run; Claude failure event supported. Exact configuration hashes and explicit absolute cwd authorize execution; scripts/dependencies remain the reviewer responsibility. Unsupported events/handler controls fail closed. Local package support is hooks only, other recognized components warn. extras/hooks.md records event mappings and limitations.',
		'Review invariant: never silently feed incompatible file-policy input to a foreign hook. Single READ adds absolute file_path; matching foreign hooks for batch/URL READ, EDIT including Write/apply_patch aliases, or GREP fail before tool execution. Hook exit2 preserves both output streams; concurrent success context remains when another handler fails. Process-group cancellation terminates children. Lifecycle state is a WeakMap tied to open session metadata; no growing global session registry.'
	],
	needs: ['an']
}
